# The red, before the fix, on the base's own source. The tree is `impl/land` at `9aac0236`, whose `tools/loop/`
# is the base `ae2373cb`'s: this item's fix was not applied when these ran.

## 1. The new case, with only the two test files checked out from the fix commit `4d1dea06` over that base

$ git checkout 4d1dea06 -- tools/loop/tests/loop-cases.sh tools/loop/tests/loop-mutations.sh
$ bash tools/loop/tests/loop-selftest.sh --case 'run#aReviewThatNamedNothingTakesNoSecondRound'
run#aReviewThatNamedNothingTakesNoSecondRound|   a report that counted a finding and named none bought a second review round
--- run#aReviewThatNamedNothingTakesNoSecondRound[0] (exit 1)
  a report that counted a finding and named none bought a second review round
FAIL run#aReviewThatNamedNothingTakesNoSecondRound
loop-selftest: 1 of 1 cases failed
exit 1

The two files were then restored to the base (`git checkout HEAD -- tools/loop/tests/loop-cases.sh
tools/loop/tests/loop-mutations.sh`) and `git status --porcelain -uall` was empty before the fix was applied.

## 2. The arm this landing added, red against the reviewed parse `'^BLOCKING:'` before it was widened

The reason it is an arm and not a case of its own (issue #1085, the correction this landing carries): the
reviewed reader missed a finding written with markdown around it, and the archive writes it that way —
`1042/reviewer-report-1-restart.md` states `LOOP-BLOCKING: 1` and puts its one finding on lines 19 and 118 as
`**BLOCKING: the delta's scenario …**`, and the round after it passed. Read as "named nothing", that report's
round would be skipped. This is `blocking_findings()` with the reviewed pattern, before the widening:

$ bash tools/loop/tests/loop-selftest.sh --case 'run#aReviewThatNamedNothingTakesNoSecondRound'
run#aReviewThatNamedNothingTakesNoSecondRound|   a refusal that named its finding in bold bought no second review round
--- run#aReviewThatNamedNothingTakesNoSecondRound[0] (exit 1)
  a refusal that named its finding in bold bought no second review round
FAIL run#aReviewThatNamedNothingTakesNoSecondRound
loop-selftest: 1 of 1 cases failed
exit 1

The pattern was then widened to `'^[[:space:]>*_]*BLOCKING:'` and the same case is green (`evidence/green.log`,
its first block).
